<h2 id="what-hidden-costs-should-i-watch-for" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-14">What hidden costs should I watch for?</h2>
<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 mb-8"><li class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700"><strong>Visa.</strong> Many travelers qualify for China's visa-free policy or the 240-hour transit exemption — if that's you, skip the visa entirely and just fill out the arrival card on the plane. See our <a href="/en/visa/visa-free/" class="text-blue-600 underline decoration-blue-300 hover:decoration-blue-600">Visa-Free Guide</a> to check whether your passport qualifies. If you do need a visa, the official application portal is <a href="https://cova.mfa.gov.cn/" class="text-blue-600 underline decoration-blue-300 hover:decoration-blue-600">cova.mfa.gov.cn</a> — current fees by nationality are listed on your local Chinese embassy's site.</li>
<li class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700"><strong>VPN.</strong> You will need one — Google, WhatsApp, Instagram, and Facebook are blocked in China, and none of them work without it. Good services cost ¥72–¥108 ($10–$15)/month. See our <a href="/en/life/vpn-guide/" class="text-blue-600 underline decoration-blue-300 hover:decoration-blue-600">VPN Guide for China</a> for choosing a stable and reliable VPN.</li>
<li class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700"><strong>Travel insurance.</strong> Foreign visitors aren't covered by China's public health insurance — hospital care is pay-as-you-go, and while a routine GP visit is cheap, an accident or emergency (surgery, hospital stays, ambulance) can run into thousands of dollars billed directly to you. Travel insurance costs ¥216–¥432 ($30–$60) for a 10-day trip and covers medical bills plus trip disruption. See our <a href="/en/life/travel-insurance/" class="text-blue-600 underline decoration-blue-300 hover:decoration-blue-600">Travel Insurance Guide</a> for how to compare plans.</li>
<li class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700"><strong>Domestic flights.</strong> Flying between cities runs about ¥576-¥1,440 ($80-$200) per leg.</li>
<li class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700"><strong>SIM card / eSIM.</strong> A 15-day data plan runs about ¥72-¥144 ($10-$20).</li>
<li class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700"><strong>SIM card / eSIM.</strong> Without data on your phone, almost nothing works. A 15-day data plan runs about ¥72–¥144 ($10–$20). See our <a href="/en/life/sim-card-guide/" class="text-blue-600 underline decoration-blue-300 hover:decoration-blue-600">SIM & eSIM Guide</a> for how to choose and set one up before you land.</li></ul>

